  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.5,
      "end": 2.1159999999999997,
      "text": "You press send max."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.116,
      "end": 5.747,
      "text": "But what happens when the fee comes from that same balance?"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.002000000000001,
      "end": 11.193000000000001,
      "text": "On Arc, the money and the gas are the same USDC."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.193000000000001,
      "end": 14.027800000000001,
      "text": "Every transaction needs a network fee,"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.0278,
      "end": 16.788,
      "text": "paid from the balance you're sending."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.788,
      "end": 21.252000000000002,
      "text": "Try to send every cent, and nothing is left to pay for it."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.528,
      "end": 25.612321428571427,
      "text": "LastDollar shows what you can actually send,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.612321428571427,
      "end": 27.15448214285714,
      "text": "what the fee may cost,"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.15448214285714,
      "end": 30.378999999999998,
      "text": "and what remains, before you approve anything."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.645999999999997,
      "end": 36.387,
      "text": "This is the live app on Arc mainnet, with real USDC."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.387,
      "end": 38.49005063291139,
      "text": "I am connected with MetaMask,"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.49005063291139,
      "end": 42.116,
      "text": "using a small wallet that holds about three cents."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.116,
      "end": 45.018,
      "text": "I will send its maximum to my other wallet."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.28399999999999,
      "end": 49.74499999999999,
      "text": "I choose Send maximum, and native USDC."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.745,
      "end": 53.18282352941176,
      "text": "LastDollar estimates the real transaction,"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.18282352941176,
      "end": 58.094,
      "text": "sets aside a maximum fee budget, and offers everything else."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.093999999999994,
      "end": 61.56099999999999,
      "text": "The estimated fee is what it will probably cost."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.56099999999999,
      "end": 64.06099999999999,
      "text": "The budget is the most it can cost."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.314,
      "end": 69.03284210526316,
      "text": "Because the real fee is usually below the budget,"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.03284210526316,
      "end": 71.082,
      "text": "a tiny amount stays behind."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.082,
      "end": 73.3960923076923,
      "text": "LastDollar says so up front,"
    },
    {
      "start": 73.3960923076923,
      "end": 76.454,
      "text": "instead of promising an empty wallet."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.72,
      "end": 79.694,
      "text": "Before anything is signed,"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.694,
      "end": 82.655,
      "text": "I confirm the recipient and the amount."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.655,
      "end": 88.012,
      "text": "When I continue, LastDollar rechecks my balance, nonce and fees."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.012,
      "end": 91.806,
      "text": "If anything changed, it would ask me to review again."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.078,
      "end": 95.959,
      "text": "Then I approve the payment in MetaMask."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.22800000000001,
      "end": 98.32300000000001,
      "text": "Confirmed."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.32300000000001,
      "end": 101.35900000000001,
      "text": "LastDollar reads the receipt from the chain."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.35900000000001,
      "end": 104.6758617886179,
      "text": "The recipient got exactly the reviewed amount,"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.6758617886179,
      "end": 106.0458699186992,
      "text": "and the actual fee,"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.0458699186992,
      "end": 110.22800000000001,
      "text": "less than a twentieth of a cent, stayed inside the budget."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.22800000000001,
      "end": 114.21600000000001,
      "text": "What is left in the wallet is the unused part of that budget."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.49000000000001,
      "end": 118.10300000000001,
      "text": "Anyone can check it on the Arc explorer."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.10300000000001,
      "end": 121.22796153846154,
      "text": "The proof page lists the mainnet payments,"
    },
    {
      "start": 121.22796153846156,
      "end": 125.84100000000002,
      "text": "and re-verifies each one live from the chain, in your browser."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.10400000000001,
      "end": 129.24755555555558,
      "text": "LastDollar is open source,"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.24755555555558,
      "end": 134.52400000000003,
      "text": "with a TypeScript SDK so other Arc apps can use the same checks."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.52400000000003,
      "end": 137.42600000000002,
      "text": "Try it at lastdollar dot vercel dot app."
    }
  ],
  "endCard": {
